# Deploy package location

Never copy, write, or unzip deployment files to:

- The Desktop (`C:\Users\lrn\Desktop` or `[Environment]::GetFolderPath("Desktop")`)
- `E:\LRN-GitHub\2026\LRNDevTeam\LabMetricsDashboard\publish`
- Any other Git-connected project `publish` folder

Put staging output, zips, overlays, SQL packs, and `DEPLOY.txt` under:

`E:\LRN-GitHub\2026\Publish`

Use subfolders such as `staging\`, `zips\`, and `backups\`.

Deploy directly to `E:\LRN-Data\PayerPolicy_v2\2026\DeploymentChanges-2026\LabMetricsApplication\LrnMetric` only when the user requests a localhost application deployment. Preserve its `appsettings*.json` and `web.config`.

# Server (Live) packages

Live packages go to `C:\LRN-Files\Deployment\ToServer` (folder + matching zip).

- Use a short name: `LRN-yyyyMMdd-HHmm` (e.g. `LRN-20261014-1519`). Do not put labs or change descriptions in the name; `DEPLOY.txt` describes the contents.
- Before creating a new package, move every existing package (folder and zip) in `ToServer` into `ToServer\Archive`, so `ToServer` only holds the latest package.
